    "result_text": "The build passes. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec required membership **level 4** to be reachable only via **tenure of more than 365 days**, so a brand-new owner (zero tenure) tops out at level 3. Previously `MembershipLevel` hard-capped at 3 with a \"reserved for tenure\" comment but no actual tenure rule.\n\n**New `util/Tenure.java`** \u2014 a small single-responsibility class computing an owner's tenure in whole days (`registrationDate` \u2192 today), returning `0` when unmeasurable. Tenure is the one derived value that depends on the current date, so it lives on its own rather than muddying the pure scoring rule.\n\n**`util/MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 added a `TENURE_DAYS = 365` threshold, raised `CAP` to 4, and added one factor: `+1` when `Tenure.days(owner) > 365`. The pre-tenure factors (base + email + unique name) still max at 3, so level 4 always requires tenure. A new owner registered today gets `0` tenure days \u2192 no bonus \u2192 level 3.\n\n**Docs kept in sync** \u2014 the Javadoc on `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel` and the `membershipLevel` schema in `openapi.yml` (range and description, now `1..4`).\n\n## Verification\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**. The acceptance test `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` (new owner with email + no namesake) asserts `membershipLevel == 3` and passes; the audit log confirms the created owner is `membershipLevel=3`.",
